  era: "Section 4 \xB7 Religious Movements \xB7 6th \u2013 5th century BCE onwards"
  title: Jain sects
  text: Jainism divided into the Digambaras, the sky-clad, whose monks renounce clothing, and the Shvetambaras, the white-clad. Tradition links the split to a famine in Magadha and the migration of the monk Bhadrabahu's followers to the south.
